DATABASE_URL=postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/olist

Or, if your code uses separate variables:
DB_USER=your_username
DB_PASSWORD=your_password
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=olist

Then build the engine like this:
import os
from dotenv import load_dotenv
from sqlalchemy import create_engine

load_dotenv()

engine = create_engine(
    f"postgresql+psycopg2://{os.getenv('DB_USER')}:{os.getenv('DB_PASSWORD')}"
    f"@{os.getenv('DB_HOST')}:{os.getenv('DB_PORT')}/{os.getenv('DB_NAME')}"
)

* Use only one of the two formats. The single DATABASE_URL is simpler.
* Commit .env.example with placeholder values only. Create your real .env locally with your actual password. It is already in .gitignore.
* If your password contains special characters like @ or #, URL-encode them (e.g. @ becomes %40) in the DATABASE_URL format.
* If you ever committed a real password earlier, change it. Deleting the file later does not remove it from Git history.
